"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nI started reading this book after being impressed by Renjo Mikihiko's  and wanting to explore more of his work.  \nI didn't realize it was a short story collection, so I spent a lot of effort taking notes on all the characters as I read. I was a bit disappointed when I realized they were short stories...  \n\nThey were typical Japanese mystery novels focused on finding motives and tricks.  \nHowever, the collection was full of short stories that evoked the same intense curiosity about the tricks as  did.  \n"